@doc <PREFIX>-STANDARDS [std, active, agents+employees, machine-drafted] v1
## <Coding standards in one line: repo-specific deltas only; shared standards referenced, not duplicated.>
@links <PREFIX>-ARCH
@cycle 90d
@reviewed <YYYY-MM-DD>

# NOTE: STANDARDS carries no spatial @anchor. Its scope is ~every source file in the repo;
# anchoring it would make coverage meaningless and flood the Layer 1 index.

@def standards-scope
  This document carries only deltas specific to <repo-name>. The binding shared engineering
  standards live in <where>; read those first — they are authoritative and are not duplicated here.

@props shared-standards
  + <STD-ID>  | <what it governs> (binding)
  + <STD-ID>  | <what it governs> (binding)

@rules
  1. <A rule that is true here and not everywhere. If it would apply to any repo, it belongs in the shared standard, not here.>
  2. <A convention an agent would otherwise violate: tenancy binding, config-as-source-of-truth, immutability.>
  3. <A fail-safe: what to do at a boundary condition rather than guessing.>

@disallowed
  ! <a pattern that is specifically wrong in this repo>
  ! <another>
